WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Speaker 1: We must follow up. I am driven.&nbsp;
I am determined to follow up about a story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.640
that is increasingly smelling like Watergate.&nbsp;
Yesterday, I told you about these roughly seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.800
hours of missing call logs that the Trump White&nbsp;
House has turned over to the January 6th Committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.640
investigating the Trump riots. So to reset the&nbsp;
entire thing and get everybody on the same page&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:29.680
for a period of time now. The January 6th&nbsp;
Committee has been wanting the logs of who did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:37.120
Donald Trump speak to on January 6th. And it turns&nbsp;
out that what was provided to the investigative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.600
committee is missing seven hours. And as I told&nbsp;
you yesterday, this was during some very key hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:52.480
between 11:17 a.m. and 6:54 p.m. This is the most&nbsp;
important time of the riots. It's from just before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:59.280
they started heading towards the Capitol through&nbsp;
the period of time during which we now know Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.120
was being urged even by people in his family, like&nbsp;
Ivanka to call in the National Guard, tell people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.880
to go home to the point at which Donald Trump&nbsp;
gave that very mealy mouthed and soft and squishy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.520
appeal to his followers to go home, even though&nbsp;
they were completely right to be there. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.400
the election, after all, was stolen. As Trump said&nbsp;
through to when people actually started leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.480
the Capitol. This is the key time we're going to&nbsp;
follow up in a moment on Donald Trump's claim that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:32.560
he doesn't know what a burner phone is because one&nbsp;
of the aspects of this is not only our seven hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:38.400
missing. Even if Trump didn't make any phone&nbsp;
calls on White House phones during that time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.120
he clearly was talking to people and he may have&nbsp;
been using burner phones. We're going to follow up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.480
about that in the next segment, but the first&nbsp;
part of this is that Talking Points memo has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:55.760
done something fascinating, which is they have&nbsp;
assembled media reports where others acknowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:01.840
speaking to Trump during that time, and they are&nbsp;
now able to say with a high degree of certainty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:08.480
here are at least some of the calls missing from&nbsp;
the call logs now, whether they're missing because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:14.080
they're just missing and haven't been turned over,&nbsp;
or whether they're missing because burner phones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.560
or other people's phones were used, we don't&nbsp;
yet know, but this is very, very interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:24.960
Talking Points Memo Trump was one hundred percent&nbsp;
making phone calls during the January 6th attack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.480
Here's the list and what they've done is they've&nbsp;
assembled media reports and they've said here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:36.000
here are calls that have been acknowledged&nbsp;
which aren't recorded anywhere. So, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.680
Mike Pence, the official records turned over to&nbsp;
the committee, don't include Trump's final call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:47.440
with Mike Pence on January 6th, during which the&nbsp;
president made a last attempt to pressure Pence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:53.200
to illegally hijack the election certification&nbsp;
process. Then Pence adviser, general Keith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.320
Kellogg, testified under oath about the&nbsp;
conversation. The Washington Post reported on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.840
call Bob Woodward and Robert Costa surface to call&nbsp;
in their book peril. So that is a specific call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:10.800
with three sources that is not on the logs.&nbsp;
So that's that's a call. There's no record&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.000
of it and what the Trump administration has&nbsp;
turned over to investigators. OK, next call.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.200
House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy. We&nbsp;
know about this call. Trump had an explosive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.200
call with the House Minority Leader Kevin&nbsp;
McCarthy, right in the middle of the attack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.280
Representative Jaime Herrera, Butler confirmed&nbsp;
the call, said McCarthy briefed her on the call.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.880
That's the conversation where Trump, responding&nbsp;
to the GOP leader sounding the alarm of violence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.640
remarked, Well, Kevin, I guess the people are&nbsp;
more upset about the election than you are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:46.480
according to Butler. That's a specific call&nbsp;
that we have independently sourced. It's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.720
on the records turned over by Trump, so that's&nbsp;
another call that took place during those seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:57.520
hours. Senators Mike Lee and Tommy Tuberville,&nbsp;
Senator Mike Lee told the Salt Lake Tribune he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:03.280
got a call from Trump moments after the Capitol&nbsp;
Police stopped the Senate proceedings. I believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.000
that was around 1:30 p.m. Eastern. I'm going. It&nbsp;
was a crazy day. I'm going from memory, but it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.160
certainly within that seven hour window of missing&nbsp;
calls. The caller ID indicated the call was coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.800
from the White House, according to Lee, but he&nbsp;
didn't know it was Trump until he picked up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:25.760
According to Lee, Trump mis dialed and was trying&nbsp;
to call Senator Tommy Tuberville. So hand that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.320
phone to the Alabama senator in the wake of the&nbsp;
attack, Tuberville revealed he told Trump in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:37.600
call that Pence was being evacuated. Third call&nbsp;
missing from the logs. Trump was on the phone this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.320
call from the White House, so this was not with a&nbsp;
burner phone. The caller ID was the White House.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:48.400
Jim Jordan, now this one we've spoken about so&nbsp;
many times and Jim Jordan has been extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:54.160
dishonest and deceptive about how many times did&nbsp;
you speak to Trump on that day? The official call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.160 --> 00:05:00.640
logs include one call between Trump and&nbsp;
Jordan at 9:24 a.m. We now know with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:06.960
benefit of hindsight. Jordan has admitted to&nbsp;
more than one call that day, and at least one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:12.640
was during the attack. So at minimum, we know&nbsp;
that there is one acknowledged Jim Jordan call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.000
not reflected in the records turned over by&nbsp;
Trump. And then lastly, Congressman Matt Gaetz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.360
Politico, reported that Gates was&nbsp;
on one of Jordan's calls to Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:30.400
during which they urged Trump to call off the&nbsp;
supporters storming the building. So that is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.440
Gates himself has refused to say if he was part&nbsp;
of the call. But Politico? He hasn't denied it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:41.120
and Politico has reported it. So again, that if&nbsp;
that's with Jim Jordan and during the attacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:48.000
it's during that seven hour window. These are&nbsp;
all easily verified by public statements. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:53.120
of course, I don't know if and how Republicans&nbsp;
will even try to spin this. They will probably say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:58.720
it's a fishing expedition. This is a bad faith&nbsp;
committee. It's a committee that needs to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.640
ended its politically oriented because they&nbsp;
don't have any Republicans other than two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.640
anti-Trump Republicans. That's because they refuse&nbsp;
to be on it. Everybody else refused to be on it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:12.160
So we do have the ability to figure out at least&nbsp;
some of these calls. Records can be cross-checked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:18.880
and then from the standpoint of the investigative&nbsp;
committee, if they successfully subpoena the phone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:25.520
records of the people on the other ends of these&nbsp;
phone calls, then they would be able to say, Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:32.160
here's a call in Jim Jordan's phone log. And it's&nbsp;
not reflected in what the White House gave us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:38.400
That's a call that they have hidden from us.&nbsp;
So clearly, that's something that they can do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.880
and this is thinking more and more like&nbsp;
like Watergate, and we're going to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.040
about that a little later. Let's now dig in&nbsp;
a little bit to the whole burner phone thing

